    {
      "coptic": "ⲉⲧⲉⲧⲛϣⲁⲛⲡⲁⲣⲁⲃⲁ ϭⲉ ⲛⲛⲁⲉⲛⲧⲟⲗⲏ · ⲡⲉⲓⲛⲟϭ ⲙⲙⲁ ϯⲛⲁⲛⲟϫϥ ⲉⲃⲟⲗ ⲙⲙⲟⲓ · ⲛⲥⲉϣⲣϣⲱⲣϥ ⲁⲩⲱ ⲛϥϣⲱⲡⲉ ⲛϫⲁⲓⲉ ⲛⲧⲉⲛⲉⲧⲡⲁⲣⲁⲅⲉ ⲧⲏⲣⲟⲩ ⲣϣⲡⲏⲣⲉ ⲛⲥⲉϣϭⲁϭⲓϫ · ⲁⲩⲱ ⲛⲥⲉ**ϣⲙϣⲏϭⲉ** ⲛⲥⲉϫⲟⲟⲥ ϫⲉⲉⲧⲃⲉⲟⲩ ⲁⲩⲉⲓⲣⲉ ϩⲓⲛⲁⲓ ⲙⲡⲉⲓⲛⲟϭ ⲙⲙⲁ",
      "english": "If, however, thou transgress My commandments, I will cast away this great place from Me, and it shall be destroyed and become such a wilderness that all those who shall pass by it shall marvel, and shall smite together their hands, and shall whistle, and shall say, 'Why have these things happened to this great place?'",
      "source": "On the End of the World and on Temple of Solomon",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:psbasil.temple.budge:1-47",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲁⲩⲱ ⲛⲧⲁⲕⲁ ⲧⲉⲓⲡⲟⲗⲓⲥ ⲉⲩⲧⲁⲕⲟ ⲙⲛⲟⲩ**ϣⲙϣⲏϭⲉ** ...",
      "english": "And I will bring this city to desolation and make it a hissing; every one that passes by it shall scowl, and hiss because of all her plague.",
